#: ../../source/algorithms/skipping.rst:4
msgid "Skipping Algorithms in Federated Learning"
msgstr "联邦学习中的跳步算法"

#: ../../source/algorithms/skipping.rst:6
msgid "Even the earliest federated learning algorithm, ``FedAvg`` [:footcite:ct:`mcmahan2017fed_avg`], performs multiple gradient-descent steps in the local inner loop of its clients -- which, in a sense, is already a *skipping* update: the communication round is skipped with probability :math:`1 - p = 0`. The ``ProxSkip`` algorithm [:footcite:ct:`proxskip,proxskip-vr`] (named ``Scaffnew`` in the original paper) studies the skipping technique systematically and makes the communication round skipped with a *nonzero* probability. It is instructive to read ``ProxSkip`` as ``SCAFFOLD`` combined with the skipping technique."
msgstr "最早的联邦学习算法 ``FedAvg`` [:footcite:ct:`mcmahan2017fed_avg`] 在子节点的内循环中执行多步梯度下降——从某种意义上说，这已经是一种* 跳步* (Skipping) 更新：通信轮以概率 :math:`1 - p = 0` 被跳过。 ``ProxSkip`` 算法 [:footcite:ct:`proxskip,proxskip-vr`]（原文献中命名为 ``Scaffnew`` ）系统地研究了跳步技术在联邦学习优化算法中的应用，使通信轮以* 非零* 的概率被跳过。将 ``ProxSkip`` 视作 ``SCAFFOLD`` 结合跳步更新技术的改进算法，是不无启发的。"

#: ../../source/algorithms/skipping.rst:18
msgid "``ProxSkip``/``Scaffnew``"
msgstr "``ProxSkip``/``Scaffnew``"

#: ../../source/algorithms/skipping.rst:20
msgid "From the optimization-theoretic viewpoint, model the federated learning problem as the consensus optimization problem over the consensus set :math:`\\mathcal{E} = \\{ \\Theta \\mid \\theta_1 = \\cdots = \\theta_K \\}`,"
msgstr "从最优化的视角出发，将联邦学习问题建模为共识集 :math:`\\mathcal{E} = \\{ \\Theta \\mid \\theta_1 = \\cdots = \\theta_K \\}` 上的共识优化问题"

#: ../../source/algorithms/skipping.rst:24
msgid ""
"\\DeclareMathOperator*{\\minimize}{minimize}\n"
"\\newcommand{\\col}{\\operatorname{col}}\n"
"\\newcommand{\\R}{\\mathbb{R}}\n"
"\\newcommand{\\prox}{\\mathbf{prox}}\n"
"\n"
"\\begin{array}{cl}\n"
"\\minimize & F(\\Theta) = \\frac{1}{K} \\sum\\limits_{k=1}^K f_k(\\theta_k), \\\\\n"
"\\text{subject to} & \\Theta \\in \\mathcal{E}, \\\\\n"
"\\text{where} & \\Theta = \\col(\\theta_1, \\cdots, \\theta_K) \\in \\R^{Kd}.\n"
"\\end{array}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/algorithms/skipping.rst:38
msgid "As in the :ref:`operator splitting section <fl_alg_operator_splitting>`, one can convert this constrained problem into an unconstrained one with the indicator function :math:`\\iota_{\\mathcal{E}}` of the consensus set and split the first-order optimality condition :math:`0 \\in \\nabla F(\\Theta) + \\partial \\iota_{\\mathcal{E}}(\\Theta)`. More generally, replacing :math:`\\iota_{\\mathcal{E}}` by any CCP function :math:`g`, the fixed-point solver is the *proximal gradient descent* (ProxGD)"
msgstr "正如 :ref:`算子分裂一节 <fl_alg_operator_splitting>` 所述，可以借助共识集的示性函数 :math:`\\iota_{\\mathcal{E}}` 将该约束问题转化为无约束问题，并对其一阶最优性条件 :math:`0 \\in \\nabla F(\\Theta) + \\partial \\iota_{\\mathcal{E}}(\\Theta)` 进行分裂。更一般地，把 :math:`\\iota_{\\mathcal{E}}` 换成任意 CCP 函数 :math:`g` ，相应的不动点求解方法即* 临近梯度下降* (Proximal Gradient Descent, ProxGD)"

#: ../../source/algorithms/skipping.rst:45
msgid "\\Theta^{(t+1)} = \\prox_{s g}\\left( \\Theta^{(t)} - s \\nabla F(\\Theta^{(t)}) \\right),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/algorithms/skipping.rst:50
msgid "for the problem :math:`\\minimize \\ F(\\Theta) + g(\\Theta)`. The practical difficulty of ProxGD is that the proximal operator :math:`\\prox_{s g}` of the CCP function :math:`g` is typically expensive to evaluate [:footcite:ct:`friedlander2017efficient`]. In federated learning, this proximal step *is* the communication: the model aggregation from the clients to the server followed by the broadcast back. Skipping this performance-bottleneck step with some probability is therefore a natural remedy, and this is exactly what ``ProxSkip`` does."
msgstr "对问题 :math:`\\minimize \\ F(\\Theta) + g(\\Theta)` 而言，ProxGD 的实际困难在于 CCP 函数 :math:`g` 的临近算子 :math:`\\prox_{s g}` 通常求解代价高昂 [:footcite:ct:`friedlander2017efficient`]。对应到联邦学习中，这一临近步* 正是* 通信本身：先由子节点向中心节点聚合模型参数，再由中心节点向子节点广播。以一定概率跳过这一性能瓶颈步骤便是一种自然的想法——这正是 ``ProxSkip`` 所做的事情。"

#: ../../source/algorithms/skipping.rst:57
msgid "A remark on the control variates: unlike ``SCAFFOLD``, ``ProxSkip`` does not use (explicit) gradient variance reduction. The primary role of the control variates :math:`c_k` is to guarantee the *correct convergence* of the overall iteration: one can show :math:`c_k \\to \\nabla f_k(\\theta^*)` at a solution :math:`\\theta^*` of the original problem, so the fixed point of the iteration is a solution of the problem -- this is the key property. ``ProxSkip`` maintains no global control variate communicated between the server and the clients; instead, whenever a communication happens, the local control variate :math:`c_k` is *implicitly* updated by :math:`\\frac{p}{\\gamma} \\left( \\theta^{(t+1)} - \\theta_k^{(t + \\frac{1}{2})} \\right)`, which acts as a global control variate. This is reminiscent of the Option II update rule of the local control variates in ``SCAFFOLD``: it saves the extra parameter exchange between the server and the clients, at the cost of the flexibility of the control variate updates. The pseudocode is summarized below."
msgstr "关于控制变量 (Control Variates) 的说明：与 ``SCAFFOLD`` 不同， ``ProxSkip`` 并未（显式地）使用梯度方差缩减技术。控制变量 :math:`c_k` 的首要作用是保证整体迭代的* 正确收敛性* ：可以证明在原问题的解点 :math:`\\theta^*` 处 :math:`c_k \\to \\nabla f_k(\\theta^*)` ，从而迭代的稳定点即为原问题的解点——这是 ``ProxSkip`` 的关键所在。 ``ProxSkip`` 整体上并不维护一个在中心节点与子节点之间通信的全局控制变量；相反，每当通信发生时，子节点上的局部控制变量 :math:`c_k` 会由 :math:`\\frac{p}{\\gamma} \\left( \\theta^{(t+1)} - \\theta_k^{(t + \\frac{1}{2})} \\right)` * 隐式* 地更新，后者起到了全局控制变量的作用。这一点类似于 ``SCAFFOLD`` 中局部控制变量的 Option II 更新规则：好处是省去了中心节点与子节点之间额外的参数传递，代价是损失了控制变量更新方法的灵活性。伪代码总结如下。"

